plasma-visual-screensaver (0.7.0-1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Move Slithering Snakes simulation and AI from QML JavaScript to a
    zero-dependency Rust library driven natively from C++, reducing CPU use
    and removing the Canvas fallback.
  * Improve pathfinding, collision avoidance, and open-space awareness.
    Bigger snakes contest food and cut rivals off, while smaller snakes
    avoid losing head-on encounters.
  * Keep shared snake worlds alive across monitor removal in synchronized
    and seamless modes.
  * Align presentation pacing with display refresh without drift for
    steadier frames across all visuals.
  * Add the Rust toolchain to builds and packaging, record Static-Built-Using,
    and add a frame-timing measurement harness.

 -- Matthew Stanton <stantonmatthewj@gmail.com>  Fri, 02 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0300

plasma-visual-screensaver (0.6.3-1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Reliably re-arm idle activation after dismissing the overlay on Plasma
    Wayland, regardless of whether Qt or KIdleTime receives the input first.
  * Preserve immediate recovery when the active monitor layout disappears.

 -- Matthew Stanton <stantonmatthewj@gmail.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 07:59:06 -0300

plasma-visual-screensaver (0.6.2-1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Replace Fireflies' fullscreen CPU Canvas with a batched native Qt Quick
    scene-graph renderer.
  * Preserve the existing motion, density, size, glow, and palette controls
    while sharply reducing CPU and GPU load on multi-monitor desktops.
  * Add geometry, premultiplied-alpha, resource, and three-monitor performance
    regression coverage for the Fireflies renderer.

 -- Matthew Stanton <stantonmatthewj@gmail.com>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 20:13:25 -0400

plasma-visual-screensaver (0.6.1-1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Release fullscreen scene-graph, Canvas, and allocator memory after every
    screensaver session instead of retaining it in the idle daemon.
  * Use shared cooperative Canvas rendering to avoid accumulating per-visual
    worker caches across repeated activations.
  * Improve Slithering Snakes food pursuit, stable target tracking, curved
    collision prediction, and long-snake self-escape behavior.
  * Expand deterministic behavior, resource-lifetime, and long-run benchmark
    coverage, including per-cause collision metrics.

 -- Matthew Stanton <stantonmatthewj@gmail.com>  Wed, 26 Aug 2026 08:31:25 -0400

